On Wed, 15 Jun 2005, Shedletsky wrote:

> I know there is at least one "Borg" (automated computer player) for Angband.
> Does anyone know if there is one for the current version of Nethack? I'm
> interested in setting my computer up to run the borg as a screensaver. For
> the screen saver to look cool, it would be nice to be able to set a maximum
> turns per sec speed. Is it possible to set something like this up without
> editting either the borg or nethack/angband code? Has anyone attempted this?

This idea has been discussed before, but nearly all efforts have been 
abandoned because Nethack has too many special cases.

In Angband there's a logical cycle of heading back to town every N turns 
to sell your junk and resupply, plus there are recall scrolls available to 
resolve any danger situation in about 20 turns.

If you've ever played Angband, you know that you can survive on the early 
levels indefinitely if you want, because you can keep generating 
random new levels with new low-level loot to find. Therefore an Angband 
bot can simply program itself to say something like "don't wander below 
level X until you have at least Y teleport scrolls on hand" - whereas in 
Nethack, you can't wait around forever until some item shows up. You'd 
starve.

That's why most of us here like Nethack more than Angband - it rewards 
cleverness and thinking on your feet, rather than tedium.

